    "kicker": "LET'S TALK / NEW ENQUIRIES",
    "h1": "Tell us what you want to build, improve or grow",
    "body": "You might have a complete brief, a performance problem or an idea that's still taking shape. Start with the challenge. We'll help clarify what the work could involve, which capabilities are relevant and what a practical first step looks like.\n\n**[Send a project enquiry](#enquiry-form)** · [Explore services](/services)\n\n## Get in touch\n\n### Email\n\n**[contact@digitalfalconz.com](mailto:contact@digitalfalconz.com)**  \nBest for project briefs, documents and detailed enquiries.\n\n### United Kingdom contact number\n\n**[+44 7988 594240](tel:+447988594240)**\n\n### United States contact number\n\n**[+1 929 652 4894](tel:+19296524894)**\n\n*These are contact numbers, not statements that DigitalFalconz maintains physical offices in the UK or USA. If calls are unanswered, please email your enquiry.*\n\n## Tell us about your project {#enquiry-form}\n\nA short outline is enough to begin. More context helps us identify an appropriate next step; a finished specification is not required.\n\n*Your information is used to respond to your enquiry and manage the related conversation. Review our [Privacy Policy](/privacy-policy).*\n\n## What happens after you get in touch?\n\n### 01. We review the brief\n\nWe look at the outcome you want, the scope, relevant systems and whether there is a good fit for our capabilities.\n\n### 02. We clarify the requirements\n\nFor suitable projects, we may suggest a discovery call or request a few details about timing, stakeholders, budgets and technical dependencies.\n\n### 03. We agree the next step\n\nDepending on the project, the recommendation might be a scoped proposal, website or campaign audit, paid technical discovery or a phased delivery plan.\n\n## Working across countries and time zones\n\nWe welcome enquiries from businesses in the USA, UK, Canada and other international markets. For each engagement we agree practical communication channels, meetings, review points, working arrangements and deliverable ownership.\n\n## Let's make the next move a considered one\n\nMarketing, software and AI decisions have different costs and risks. Tell us what you need to achieve. We'll discuss an appropriate starting point rather than suggest technology for its own sake.\n\n**[Email DigitalFalconz](mailto:contact@digitalfalconz.com)**",
    "title": "Contact DigitalFalconz | Marketing, Software & AI Projects",
